Translation patch: <VartimeRistrettoPrecomputation as VartimePrecomputedMultiscalarMul>::optional_mixed_multiscalar_mul (src/ristretto.rs)

Change: The lazy `dynamic_points.into_iter().map(|P_opt| P_opt.map(|P| P.0))` becomes a
`Vec<Option<EdwardsPoint>>` built by a nested helper.

Why: the Aeneas Lean library models only `Iterator::next`; the provided methods
(`map`, `zip`, `fold`, `filter`, `collect`, `rev`, `skip`, `size_hint`, `by_ref`, ...)
are missing (AeneasVerif/aeneas#1057), so the original does not build in Lean.
Aeneas also cannot extract a loop that calls `next()` directly on the `IntoIter` of a
generic `IntoIterator` parameter ("Could not find: type_var_id .. from ExtractBase.Item"),
so the consuming loop lives in a nested helper function generic over `It: Iterator`,
called with `x.into_iter()`.

Behaviour: **not identical; same result for finite inputs.** The callee receives the same `Option`s
in the same order, so it returns `None` at the same point (before its length asserts) and
otherwise the same result. Differences: the dynamic points are read eagerly, before the
callee reads any scalar; all of them are read, even after a `None` (so an element after a
`None` that panics when read now panics, where the original returned `None`); a points
iterator that is infinite after a `None` (e.g. `once(None).chain(repeat(Some(P)))`), for
which the original returned `None`, no longer terminates. `size_hint` is no longer called on
the caller's iterator.

Facts relied on (not visible in the diff): The callee (`VartimePrecomputedStraus::optional_mixed_multiscalar_mul`, all backends)
collects `static_scalars` and `dynamic_scalars` fully, then collects `dynamic_points` with
`collect::<Option<Vec<_>>>()?` (short-circuiting at the first `None`, before its length
asserts).

Remove this patch when Aeneas translates the original code: delete the file,
run ./scripts/aeneas-translate.sh and `lake build`, and check both succeed.

diff --git a/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs b/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
index 269662d..174f38b 100644
--- a/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
+++ b/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
@@ -1028,22 +1028,33 @@ fn is_empty(&self) -> bool {
     fn optional_mixed_multiscalar_mul<I, J, K>(
         &self,
         static_scalars: I,
         dynamic_scalars: J,
         dynamic_points: K,
     ) -> Option<Self::Point>
     where
         I: IntoIterator,
         I::Item: Borrow<Scalar>,
         J: IntoIterator,
         J::Item: Borrow<Scalar>,
         K: IntoIterator<Item = Option<Self::Point>>,
     {
+        fn extended_points<It>(mut points: It) -> Vec<Option<EdwardsPoint>>
+        where
+            It: Iterator<Item = Option<RistrettoPoint>>,
+        {
+            let mut out = Vec::new();
+            while let Some(P_opt) = points.next() {
+                out.push(P_opt.map(|P| P.0));
+            }
+            out
+        }
+
         self.0
             .optional_mixed_multiscalar_mul(
                 static_scalars,
                 dynamic_scalars,
-                dynamic_points.into_iter().map(|P_opt| P_opt.map(|P| P.0)),
+                extended_points(dynamic_points.into_iter()),
             )
             .map(RistrettoPoint)
     }
 }
